<title>CHILE: Colbun tumbles after privatization fails.</title>
<headline>Colbun tumbles after privatization fails.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean state-controlled power firm Colbun's shares plummeted 9.6 percent to 47 pesos on heavy volume after the government rejected all bidders for privatization of 37.5 percent of the company.</p>
<p>&quot;The market had a very different expectations,&quot; said one broker.</p>
<p>&quot;People are perplexed and everyone is asking what Colbun's real value is now. And to think it was at 53 pesos this morning,&quot; said another.</p>
<p>The state companies authority CORFO declared the tender &quot;deserted&quot; -- meaning it rejected all bids -- and said none of the offers were in line with the company's market value.</p>
<p>About 15 percent of Colbun is traded on the Santiago Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
</text>
